From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:52:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Run SuperSpeed on USB-C port 2

This is the J604 form of the board half of 3949e3640d ("arm64: apple:
enable qualified J713 SuperSpeed host support"), for one port.

Describe the seven T8132 ATC windows of ATC1 (USB-C port 2, left rear,
SN201202X hpm1 on nub SPMI A0, Type-C class port 2 in probe order) and
give its controller the USB3 PHY with maximum-speed "super-speed". With
the "common-config" window present the PHY driver takes the banked
SuperSpeed path; the calibration is the boot loader's: m1n1 copies the
J604 ADT atc-phy1 tunables into apple,tunable-usb3-{axi2af,lioa,fabric,
config,common,efuse}, apple,tunable-lane{0,1}-usb and
apple,tunable-usb3-dp on every apple,t8132-atcphy alias of an admitted
board, the J604 included. Without them the driver keeps the port at USB2
("T8132 calibration incomplete, USB2 only").

The J604 ADT places atc-phy1 at 0x40aa90000 (usb2phy), 0x40b000000/0x58000
(core, fabric, common-config and the display crossbar at +0x4c000) and
0x408000000/0x1000000 (axi2af, lioa), and usb-drd1 has the PIPE handler
at 0x40aa84000: the J713's ATC1 windows, all inside them. The crossbar
(atc1-dpxbar, 0x40b04c000) stays outside the mapped resources.

Why port 2: ATC1 is the block the J713 qualification covers (its ATC0
stays USB2 until that port's common-power handoff is qualified); the
driver refuses to start SuperSpeed on a common block that is not cold
and does not reset an inherited one. Ports 1 and 4 (ATC0, ATC3) stay
USB2 until port 2 is measured on this machine.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index afaf97dcbf..d2fee3667d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -398,7 +398,8 @@
 };
 
 /*
- * USB-C ports 1, 2 and 4 (ATC0, ATC1 and ATC3), USB2 only. The port numbers
+ * USB-C ports 1, 2 and 4 (ATC0, ATC1 and ATC3). Port 2 (ATC1) also runs
+ * SuperSpeed (5 Gbit/s host); ports 1 and 4 stay USB2 only. The port numbers
  * are the Apple device tree's, which gives number 3 to the DisplayPort PHY
  * of ATC2, not a USB-C port. The SN201202X port controllers of ports 1 and 2
  * sit on SPMI A0; the third controller on that bus (hpm5, USID 8) is the
@@ -565,6 +566,22 @@
 
 &atcphy1 {
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-USB-1a */
+	/*
+	 * SuperSpeed on USB-C port 2 (left rear) only: the ATC block the J713
+	 * qualified. All seven windows lie inside this J604's own ADT atc-phy1
+	 * and usb-drd1 ranges; the display crossbar at core + 0x4c000
+	 * (atc1-dpxbar) is left to its own driver. The calibration comes from
+	 * the boot loader (apple,tunable-usb3-*, lane0/1-usb).
+	 */
+	reg = <0x4 0x0aa90000 0x0 0x4000>,
+	      <0x4 0x0aa84000 0x0 0x4000>,
+	      <0x4 0x0b000000 0x0 0x24000>,
+	      <0x4 0x08000000 0x0 0x8000>,
+	      <0x4 0x08020000 0x0 0x4000>,
+	      <0x4 0x0b044000 0x0 0x4000>,
+	      <0x4 0x0b050000 0x0 0x4000>;
+	reg-names = "usb2phy", "pipehandler", "core", "axi2af", "lioa",
+		    "fabric", "common-config";
 
 	ports {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
@@ -589,6 +606,9 @@
 
 &dwc3_1 {
 	dr_mode = "host";
+	maximum-speed = "super-speed";
+	phys = <&atcphy1 PHY_TYPE_USB2>, <&atcphy1 PHY_TYPE_USB3>;
+	phy-names = "usb2-phy", "usb3-phy";
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-USB-1b */
 
 	ports {
